<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gollub War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1422">1422</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gollub War was a brief conflict in 1422 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and the allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, named after the town of Golub (Gollub), which the allies captured. The Order received no help from the Empire and was ravaged by the invading armies. The war ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-melno">Treaty of Melno</a>, which settled the long-disputed border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gollub-war.jpg" alt="Gollub War" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jerzy Strzelecki · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Golub4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
